Town Clerk		 
	
		 
			

		 				
	 

	 	



 
	 

		 
			 The Town Clerk is appointed by the Town Manager and holds the rank of department head.  The Town Clerk serves as the Chief Election Official, Records Access Officer, and the custodian of Town records including Vital Records and other official documents filed in the Town Clerk's Office. She is responsible for the maintenance, preservation and disposition of Town records in her custody. The Town Clerk and her staff are here to assist you with voter information, voter registration, information concerning vital records, filing intentions for Marriage Licenses, Business Certificates, Special Permits, licensing dogs, census information and many other ways.  State law provides that the Town Clerk is the keeper of the Town Seal.  
		 
	 
 

 
